  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of siting and design, would present an irregular form and appear unsympathetic to the built form and character of the semi-detached pair. Its siting on the boundary would present an adverse impact to the streets scene and would disrupt the existing planned form of development. The proposal would cause undue harm to the character and appearance of the semi-detached pair, the street scene and the planned form of the area. The proposal is therefore contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that development recognises local character and promotes good design:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021)The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)Policies SP2, DMD1, and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
